    "knowledge_point_id": "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum",
    "problem": "If the sum of the first $36$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{36}=\\frac{225}{2},$ and the last term is ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2},$ what is the first term of the series?",
    "worked_solution": "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2}$, $N=36$, and ${S}_{N}=\\frac{225}{2}$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{225}{2} & =\\frac{36}{2}({a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{225}{36} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ \\frac{25}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{25}{4}-\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
